{"analysis":{"code_ref":"train.py DIAGNOSE; diag_cap64_seg_s42.log vs diag_cap256_seg_s42.log","method":"per-decile / per-position difference, absolute AND relative"},"artifact_paths":[],"assessment":{"limitations":["absolute and relative readings disagree; proxy observable"],"relation":"inconclusive","strength":"moderate"},"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-07-22T20:25:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-observable","evidence_id":"evd_obs_capacity_decile_decomposition","experiment_id":"exp_ngram256_docmask_seg_validation","facts":{"result":"OBSERVABLE CAUSAL PROBE (obs_val_nats_by_freq_decile + obs_val_nats_by_pos_bin) via DIAGNOSE=1, seed 42: 64x+seg (val_bpb 0.928372) vs 256x+seg (0.924638). ABSOLUTE nats improvement by decile d0..d9: 0.085/0.089/0.112/0.133/0.138/0.140/0.154/0.144/0.157/0.173 -- rare(d7-d9) 0.158 vs frequent(d0-d2) 0.095 = 1.66x. BUT RELATIVE improvement is FLAT-TO-DECLINING: 5.60/4.93/5.39/5.82/4.89/4.91/4.67/4.05/4.07/4.30 % (frequent 5.26% vs rare 4.14%). A rare-specific collision-interference mechanism predicts RELATIVE gain RISING with rarity; the observed pattern is the OPPOSITE and is most consistent with a roughly UNIFORM MULTIPLICATIVE improvement, rare deciles gaining more in absolute terms only because they carry more loss. POSITION BINS: improvement flat 0.127-0.139 nats across all 8 bins (capacity is not a position mechanism; also validates the position observable can detect flatness, making it a real discriminator for the seg-mask test). CAVEAT: deciles bucket by TARGET-TOKEN frequency while collisions occur in CONTEXT space -- proxy only, does not settle the mechanism."},"fingerprint":"1667644a652f41e4","hypothesis_ids":["hyp_ngram256_docmask_seg"],"paper_ids":[],"run_ids":["run_exp_ngram256_docmask_cap256_s46_a42bb3feafcf9a3c","run_exp_ngram256_docmask_cap256_s47_ba1f82f731fb6e27","run_exp_ngram256_docmask_cap256_s48_694a943b68a90566","run_exp_ngram256_docmask_cap256_docseg_s46_2b7e72353d053fd4","run_exp_ngram256_docmask_cap256_docseg_