{"analysis":{"code_ref":"NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT sweep on SOTA #4","method":"paired-t per arm vs 256x control, 3 seeds"},"artifact_paths":[],"assessment":{"limitations":["384x is directionally negative but mixed-sign and sub-threshold"],"relation":"inconclusive","strength":"moderate"},"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-07-23T01:00:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_id":"evd_run_fourgram_capacity_sweep","experiment_id":"exp_fourgram_capacity_sweep","facts":{"result":"4-GRAM CAPACITY SWEEP on SOTA #4, 3 paired seeds per arm, control = 4-gram@256x (mean 0.923852). 384x: deltas -0.00046/+0.00015/-0.00057, mean -0.000294, MIXED sign, t=-1.31 -> NULL, fails the -0.001 funnel: no gain from MORE 4-gram capacity. 128x: deltas +0.00048/+0.00053/+0.00022, mean +0.000407, 3/3 WORSE, t=4.19 -> capacity CANNOT be reclaimed for free. Capacity curve 128x=0.924259 / 256x=0.923852 / 384x=0.923558. CONCLUSION: 256x sits at the knee for the 4-gram ORDER, mirroring the base bigram/trigram capacity axis which also saturated between 256x and 384x (-0.000611, sub-threshold). Both the base tables and the newly-restored 4-gram order share the same capacity optimum, which is a coherent picture: capacity helps up to ~256x and then stops paying, independent of n-gram order."},"fingerprint":"6982ba213ec4bf23","hypothesis_ids":["hyp_fourgram_capacity_sweep"],"paper_ids":[],"run_ids":["run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg256_ctrl_s42_d0006f8b3ebd0535","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg256_ctrl_s43_6378792a63247efe","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg256_ctrl_s44_80e79149ba6525fd","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg128_s42_ef53e81c1f7a91b0","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg384_s42_26ace2a2a0932caa","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg384_s43_85c80bbe454b6fcf","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg384_s44_3940689a32674115","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg128_s43_2927d5933f8ec5fb","run_exp_fourgram_capacit_fg128_s44_d3a2a6848570ddea"],"source_type":"internal_run","supersedes_evidence_id":"","tags":["ngram","fourgram","capacity","sweep","saturatin