{"analysis":{"code_ref":"NGRAM_TABLE_MULT=384 on SOTA #4","method":"paired-t vs SOTA #4, 3 seeds; magnitude compared against the pre-4-gram measurement"},"artifact_paths":[],"assessment":{"limitations":["sub-threshold in both conditions"],"relation":"inconclusive","strength":"moderate"},"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-07-23T01:35:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_id":"evd_run_base_capacity_x_fourgram","experiment_id":"exp_base_capacity_x_fourgram","facts":{"result":"BASE CAPACITY 384x on SOTA #4 (which includes 4-gram@256x), 3 paired seeds: deltas -0.00044/-0.00014/-0.00014, mean -0.000240, 3/3 negative but paired-t=-2.43, FAILS the -0.001 funnel. INTERACTION READING: base capacity 256->384 measured WITHOUT 4-gram was -0.000611; measured WITH 4-gram it is -0.000240 (difference +0.000371). Both are small, sub-threshold, and of the same sign/order of magnitude, so the two axes are essentially INDEPENDENT -- adding the 4-gram order does not materially change how much extra base capacity is worth, and vice versa. Combined with the 4-gram capacity sweep (its own knee also at 256x), the picture is: capacity and order are SEPARABLE axes, each saturating on its own schedule, and base capacity is saturated at 256x whether or not the 4-gram order is present."},"fingerprint":"2f009ba232e0d5cd","hypothesis_ids":["hyp_base_capacity_x_fourgram"],"paper_ids":[],"run_ids":["run_exp_base_capacity_x__sota004_s43_3f591553167675f4","run_exp_base_capacity_x__sota004_s42_cb595ba050b5a0ba","run_exp_base_capacity_x__sota004_s44_71fccd4b9cf85cc0","run_exp_base_capacity_x__base384_s42_fbc55f05e5eaab70","run_exp_base_capacity_x__base384_s43_2dbe4fa552e71a85","run_exp_base_capacity_x__base384_s44_ddd9e36bda0ace82"],"source_type":"internal_run","supersedes_evidence_id":"","tags":["ngram","capacity","interaction","null","saturating"],"trust":{"design":"strong","directness":"strong","limitations":["3 seeds","the pre-4-gram comparison used a different control config, so the intera