{"analysis": {"code_ref": "EXPLORE:NGRAM_FIVEGRAM, NGRAM_FIVEGRAM_MULT=256", "method": "paired-t over 3 seed deltas vs SOTA #4; compared against the 4-gram rung's measured effect"}, "artifact_paths": [], "assessment": {"limitations": ["3 seeds only -- the screen is powered for a -0.001 effect, not for resolving a -0.0005 one", "cannot distinguish 'no 5th-order signal' from 'signal unlearnable at this token budget'"], "relation": "opposes", "strength": "moderate"}, "claim_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-07-23T02:05:00-07:00", "created_by": "claude-ledger", "evidence_id": "evd_run_fivegram_order", "experiment_id": "exp_fivegram_order", "facts": {"result": "5-GRAM VE @256x added on top of SOTA #4 (256x base + seg + warmdown 0.75 + 4-gram@256x), 3 paired seeds 42/43/44: deltas -0.000763 / -0.000662 / +0.000015, mean -0.000470, sd 0.000423, paired-t = -1.92, 2/3 negative. FAILS the -0.001 advance gate and is well below the 2-sigma seed floor of 0.001694. NOT advanced to hold-out. ORDER LADDER SHAPE: the per-rung marginal gain decays cleanly -- 4-gram gave -0.001307 (6/6 hold-out seeds, t=-26.27), 5-gram gives -0.000470 (2/3, t=-1.92), roughly a 2.8x drop. The point estimate is directionally favourable, so this is a DIMINISHING-RETURNS termination, not evidence that 5th-order context carries no information. LIKELY MECHANISM, stated as interpretation not measurement: with only 294.9M training tokens in a single ~0.47-epoch pass, the overwhelming majority of distinct 5-grams are seen once or never, so a hashed 5-gram value embedding has too few repeat observations per bucket to learn a useful vector within 2000 steps. That is a DATA-BUDGET limit, not an architectural verdict: under a longer budget or more tokens the 5-gram rung might well pay. Cost note: 5-gram ON runs at 87.2 GB vs 76.6 GB for SOTA #4, so the rung also costs +10.6 GB for a sub-threshold return."}, "fingerprint": "e0b7e1e6adfeb201", "hypothesis_ids": ["hyp_fivegram_order"], "paper_ids": [], "run_ids": ["run_e