{"analysis": {"code_ref": "EXPLORE:NGRAM_FOURGRAM_SPAN, NGRAM_FOURGRAM_SPAN=4", "method": "paired-t over 3 seed deltas; controls REUSED from exp_fivegram_order's sota004 arm (identical config and seeds); 95% CI via t_{0.975,df=2}=4.303"}, "artifact_paths": [], "assessment": {"limitations": ["3 seeds; CI spans both rival hypotheses, so only the extreme (range-decay) branch is decided", "controls were reused rather than re-run concurrently"], "relation": "mixed", "strength": "moderate"}, "claim_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-07-23T03:55:00-07:00", "created_by": "claude-ledger", "evidence_id": "evd_run_gappy_fourgram_dose", "experiment_id": "exp_gappy_fourgram_dose", "facts": {"result": "GAPPY 4-gram (w[-4],w[-2],w[-1],w[0]) vs contiguous 4-gram (w[-3],w[-2],w[-1],w[0]) inside SOTA #4, 3 paired seeds: -0.000190 / +0.000237 / +0.000371, mean +0.000139, sd 0.000293, paired-t = +0.82, 2/3 positive. NULL: the gappy context performs the SAME as the contiguous one. 95% CI on the delta = [-0.000589, +0.000867]. WHAT THIS RULES OUT (the clean result): RANGE DECAY is EXCLUDED. If the adjacent position w[-3] carried information that w[-4] could not substitute for, dropping it should have cost most of the 4-gram rung's value (+0.0012); that value lies OUTSIDE the CI. So the 4-gram win does NOT depend on strict contiguity -- the model is exploiting the existence of a 4-token conjunction, not its adjacency structure. WHAT THIS CANNOT DECIDE (stated against the pre-registration): the pre-registered rule assigns a delta in [0,+0.0008] to the SPARSITY-MEDIATED bucket, and +0.000139 falls there, but that reading is NOT supported because the CI contains BOTH zero (no effect) AND the pure-sparsity point prediction (+0.000443). The 3-seed design is underpowered to separate them, so no mediation claim is made. TENSION WORTH RECORDING: the implied per-singleton-point slope is 3.2x shallower here than on the 4->5-gram step (0.0096e-3 vs 0.0305e-3 per point). Taken at face value that would argue singleton rate is NOT a sufficient mediator of the order ceiling, but at t=0.82 the gappy slope is not resolved from zero, so this is a flag for a better-powered test rather than a finding."}, "fingerprint": "a3ead34251fe85c4", "hypothesis_ids": ["hyp_gappy_fourgram_sparsity_dose"], "paper_ids": [], "run_ids": ["run_exp_gappy_fourgram_d_gappy4_s42_64a8f1184f4a687a", "run_exp_gappy_fourgram_d_gappy4_s43_d4c6f50fb81f5fc5", "run_exp_gappy_fourgram_d_gappy4_s44_2f14a4ff40e3834b", "run_exp_fivegram_order_sota004_s42_04a048e19d2fd122", "run_exp_fivegram_order_sota004_s43_472a14999b061740", "run_exp_fivegram_order_sota004_s44_50340ae6861c76b3"], "source_type": "internal_run", "supersedes_evidence_id": "", "tags": ["ngram", "fourgram", "context_shape", "gappy", "dose_response", "null", "underpowered"], "trust": {"design": "strong", "directness": "strong", "limitations": ["Reused controls come from train.py v10 while the treatment ran v11; justified by evd_obs_pipeline_not_bitwise_deterministic, which showed v10 differs from ITSELF by 0.001758 vs the 0.001783 v10-v11 gap, so the code change is inert. Residual risk is ordinary run-to-run noise, already inside the modelled floor.", "Underpowered for the intended mediation contrast."], "replication": "adequate", "scope_match": "strong"}}
{"analysis":{"code_ref":"pre-fix train.py: WARMUP_RATIO referenced only at definition, _envf resolution, and the RESOLVED_CONFIG f-string. post-fix train.py: warmup_lr_mult / lrm_warmup in the training loop (added 2026-07-24).","method":"Source audit of the train.py LR schedule: enumerated every reference to WARMUP_RATIO and confirmed all were assignment, env resolution, or the RESOLVED_CONFIG banner; no read reached the training loop. Retrospective re-reading of the six recorded arm configurations under that finding."},"artifact_paths":[],"assessment":{"limitations":["supersedes evd_run_ngram256_seg_warmup002, which reported a null that no experiment produced","the six underlying runs are individually valid; it is the CONTRAST between them that is void","does not itself measure warmup -- it removes a false measurement"],"relation":"not_tested","strength":"none"},"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-07-24T00:20:00-07:00","created_by":"claude-ledger","evidence_id":"evd_run_ngram256_seg_warmup002_retracted","experiment_id":"exp_ngram256_seg_warmup002_discovery","facts":{"consequence":"The WARMUP_RATIO=0.02 arms and the 256x+seg control arms trained the IDENTICAL schedule. The three paired arms differed only in a logged configuration string, so the reported deltas (-0.000006/-0.000036/-0.000154, mean -0.000065, paired-t=-1.45) measure seed-level run-to-run noise between duplicate configurations, not the effect of LR warmup.","defect":"train.py defined WARMUP_RATIO, resolved it from the environment via _envf, and printed it into RESOLVED_CONFIG, but no LR schedule code ever read it. The training loop derived every learning-rate multiplier from WARMDOWN_RATIO and ADAM_WARMDOWN_RATIO only. WARMUP_RATIO was a logging-only variable.","hypothesis_state":"hyp_ngram256_seg_warmup002 is UNTESTED. LR warmup on the frozen 2000-step challenge has never been measured.","remediation":"train.py now implements warmup: warmup_lr_mult() ramps the Muon/Adam LR multipliers from FINAL_LR_FRAC*lr to lr across [0, WARMUP_RATIO), with WARMUP_RATIO=0.0 (the frozen baseline) an exact no-op. Range validation rejects overlap with the warmdown phase. tests/test_lr_warmup.py asserts the knob is read inside the training loop, not merely logged.","what_the_deltas_actually_are":"A useful incidental measurement of same-config replicate noise at 2000 steps: |delta| <= 0.000154 across three seed pairs."},"fingerprint":"e7531608b5f00865","hypothesis_ids":["hyp_ngram256_seg_warmup002"],"paper_ids":[],"run_ids":["run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_s42_01da169403708aad","run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_wu002_s42_f186946560e84a60","run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_s43_5c13d9a378707627","run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_wu002_s43_0ea2971a2bfa1f3f","run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_s44_3372517f5e0c4a50","run_exp_ngram256_seg_war_cap256_seg_wu002_s44_8255ccf4ddc0756f"],"source_type":"offline_analysis","supersedes_evidence_id":"evd_run_ngram256_seg_warmup002","tags":["schedule","warmup","retraction","invalid","dead_knob"],"trust":{"design":"strong","directness":"strong","limitations":["static source analysis, not a re-run of the six arms"],"replication":"not_applicable","scope_match":"strong"}}
